<title>PORTUGAL: Finalists in Oporto metro project to be chosen.</title>
<headline>Finalists in Oporto metro project to be chosen.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-11-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two international consortia will be chosen this week as finalists in the public competition to build a 130 billion escudos ($850 million) urban transport system in Oporto in northern Portugal, newspapers said over the weekend.</p>
<p>The four bidding groups include GEC Alsthom/Bento Pedroso Construcoes and Somague ; Siemens /Mota &amp; Companhia/Teixeira Duarte and Engil; Spie Batignolles/Ansaldo /Bombardier and Grupo Nelson Quintas; and ABB /Soares da Costa and Assiconstroi.</p>
<p>The client, Sociedade do Metro do Porto, is expected to choose the winning bidder at the end of the first quarter next year, Publico newspaper said on Sunday.</p>
<p>Construction work is due to begin in April 1997 and the metro system should open in 2000.</p>
</text>
